W: 1. I thought I heard the skipper say,
W: Leave her Johnny, leave her!
W: "Tomorrow you will get your pay:"
W: It's time for us to leave her.
W:
W: (Refrain:)
W: Leave her, Johnny, leave her.
W: Ooh! Leave her, Johnny, leave her!
W: For the voyage is done and the winds don't blow,
W: So it's time for us to leave her.
W:
W: 2. The work was hard and the passage long,
W: Leave her Johnny, leave her!
W: The seas were high and the gales were strong.
W: It's time for us to leave her.
W: (Refrain:)
W:
W: 3. The food was bad and the wages low,
W: Leave her Johnny, leave her!
W: But now ashore again we'll go.
W: It's time for us to leave her.
W: (Refrain:)
W:
W: 4. The sails are furled and our work is done.
W: Leave her Johnny, leave her!
W: But now on shore we'll have some fun.
W: It's time for us to leave her.
W: (Refrain:)
%
